WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.980
Privacy and security in Open WebUI begin with recognizing what the system may hold:

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.665
prompts, outputs, uploaded files, conversation history, user accounts, API keys,

00:00:09.665 --> 00:00:13.920
endpoint configuration, logs, database backups, and operational metadata.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.200
Any of these may contain sensitive information.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.970
A private AI interface is still an application that needs secure operation.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:24.090
API keys and endpoint credentials should be protected because they may allow access to

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:24.875
model services,

00:00:24.875 --> 00:00:27.680
billing resources, private endpoints, or internal systems.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.100
Avoid exposing credentials in screenshots, shared notes, logs,

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.200
or configuration files with broad access.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.036
Rotate credentials when needed and remove old keys when endpoints are retired.

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:40.140
Plugin and tool features should be approached carefully at a high level.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.750
Anything that lets a model interact with external systems, files, APIs,

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:47.430
or automation increases the need for permission boundaries and review.

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:51.310
Model output should not be treated as authority to perform high-impact actions.

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:55.210
Keep tool use scoped, monitored, and appropriate to the deployment's purpose.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:59.110
Operations include updates, monitoring, backups, and incident response.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:02.760
Watch resource usage, disk growth, failed requests, unusual access,

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.230
and model endpoint errors.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:08.280
Keep the application and supporting components updated with a deliberate process.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.185
If accidental exposure or misconfiguration occurs,

00:01:11.185 --> 00:01:15.800
operators should know how to disable access, preserve evidence, rotate credentials,

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:18.240
restore from backup, and notify the right stakeholders.
